{"ts": "2026-09-21T00:55:00Z", "event": "phase_start", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 2, "task": null, "message": "Homebrew as an install method", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T01:20:00Z", "event": "issue", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 2, "task": "TASK-012", "message": "found and fixed a real ordering bug while wiring the manifest.toml overrides: graph::topo_order() computed dependency order from each Tool's BASE requires field only, never consulting platform overrides. ripgrep/direnv/delta's macOS override adds requires=[\"homebrew\"], but that edge was invisible to topo_order, so homebrew sorted alphabetically (last) instead of first -- a macOS plan would have tried to brew-install ripgrep before homebrew existed. Fixed by adding topo_order_for(tools, platform), a platform-aware variant sharing the same Kahn's-algorithm core via a generic topo_order_with(tools, requires_of) helper; graph::select() now calls topo_order_for. topo_order() (base-only) is kept for Manifest::validate()'s cycle check and existing tests, unchanged. Caught by TEST-012 and by manually testing `pinst plan --platform macos ripgrep --json`, not by the original plan text -- worth a LESSON about ordering functions needing to consult the same resolution path selection does.", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T01:21:00Z", "event": "issue", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 2, "task": "TASK-016", "message": "found and fixed a second bug from the same wiring pass: Tool::upgrade_spec_for() checked the platform override's own `upgrade` field, then unconditionally fell back to the tool's base-level `upgrade` override before deriving from the effective install. delta's base entry has an explicit `upgrade = apt` override; with the naive fallback, upgrade_spec_for(MacOS) would have returned UpgradeSpec::Apt even though the effective install is brew. Fixed: the base-level upgrade override is now only inherited when the platform override did not also replace `install` -- an explicit upgrade spec was written for a specific install method and should not silently apply to a different one. Covered by TEST-010 (manifest.rs) using the real delta entry.", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T01:22:00Z", "event": "issue", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 2, "task": "TASK-015", "message": "manifest.toml comment in phase-02.md sketched curl_script with an args=[\"NONINTERACTIVE=1\"] field for homebrew's installer, but curl_script's args are appended as positional arguments after `--`, not exported as env vars, and NONINTERACTIVE is read from the environment by Homebrew's install.sh. Used the `shell` method instead: `NONINTERACTIVE=1 /bin/bash -c \"$(curl ...)\"`, matching Homebrew's own documented one-liner. Also added an explicit `upgrade = { method = \"github_release\", repo = \"Homebrew/brew\" }` override on the tool, since Install::Shell carries no github_repo field the way CurlScript does.", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T01:25:00Z", "event": "task_done", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 2, "task": "TASK-009..016", "message": "Install::Brew/UpgradeSpec::Brew added; src/core/exec/brew.rs executor (never emits sudo); StepKind::BrewUpdate + brew:update latch mirroring apt in both build_install_plan and build_upgrade_plan; brew_latest() via `brew info --json=v2`; brew_upstream_of() strips a trailing _<digits> revision suffix before comparing versions; manifest.toml gained a `homebrew` tool (shell install, unsupported on linux) and macOS brew overrides on ripgrep, direnv and delta.", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T01:26:00Z", "event": "phase_done", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 2, "task": null, "message": "just qc green: 239 tests (12 new this phase). Manually verified with the built binary: pinst plan --platform macos --json orders homebrew before ripgrep/direnv/delta and pulls it in via explicit single-tool selection too; pinst doctor --json (linux) reports tool.unsupported.homebrew; pinst schema output/manifest still parse as JSON.", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T01:30:00Z", "event": "phase_start", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 3, "task": null, "message": "A manifest and configs that cover macOS", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T02:00:00Z", "event": "issue", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 3, "task": "TASK-015", "message": "found a real dependency cycle while wiring curl/git/unzip/zsh macOS overrides: homebrew's entry had requires=[\"curl\"] (copied from the Linux pattern), but curl's own macOS override now requires homebrew -- a two-node cycle that topo_order_for (added in phase 2) correctly rejected at runtime rather than silently misordering. Fixed by removing requires=[\"curl\"] from homebrew: macOS ships curl as part of the OS, so pinst has nothing to manage there before homebrew's own bootstrap runs. Caught immediately by running `pinst doctor --platform macos --json` against the built binary rather than only via unit tests -- worth noting for LESSON-002/LESSON-020's territory: a manifest edit that type-checks and validates can still be logically wrong, and running the actual command is what caught it.", "detail": {}}
{"ts": "2026-09-21T02:05:00Z", "event": "task_done", "plan": "260920-qcrrqs-macos-support", "phase": 3, "task": "TASK-017..024", "message": "Audited all 9 curl_script/shell installers by fetching each installer script and grepping for Darwin/macOS handling (herdr, aven, opencode, claude, oh-my-posh, uv confirmed via explicit uname branching; oh-my-zsh, nvm, rustup confirmed portable-by-construction, no OS branch needed) -- all portable as written, comments added to manifest.toml. Added macOS brew overrides for curl/git/unzip/gh/zsh/fd (fd also drops its Debian-specific post_install). build-essential marked unsupported with the xcode-select note. neovim's macOS override replaces the Linux-only github_release asset with brew. pinst's macOS override names the aarch64 Darwin asset. zsh's chsh post_install skip_if extended to also skip when the resolved zsh is absent from /etc/shells. configs/zsh/.zshrc: neovim's /opt PATH entry is now existence-guarded, and a brew shellenv eval was added, discovering the prefix (/opt/homebrew or /usr/local) rather than hard-coding it. Added docs/tools/homebrew.toml (status=draft: its brew recipes were not run on a real Mac, so 'authored' would misclaim they were) and documented the brew method + [tool.platform.<name>] override block + --platform in README.md.", "detail": {}}
